        "heading_pdyJD6": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Australian native timber plantation",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_cDbbJp": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The long-term goal for our business is to develop a sustainable native timber plantation and sawmill on our property in Coolongolook, on the mid-north coast of New South Wales. The property began to be cleared by our family in the mid-1930s to establish a dairy farm, later in the 1970s transitioning to a beef cattle farm. Now we see great value in regenerating the land as a sustainable forestry operation.</p><p><em>Our vision</em> is to establish a mixed-species native timber plantation with maintenance practiced to ensure growth of excellent quality timber, and a selective harvesting schedule that gradually transitions into a beautiful forest with a <em>commercial</em> and <em>sustainable</em> future.</p>"
          }
        }
